On 27 March 2026 at 23:44, Charles Plessy wrote:
| The simplest approach I know is to install all packages listed in the
| Suggests field of each package’s DESCRIPTION file before running 
| the tests.

[...]

| I am not fully familiar with how CRAN or upstream projects run package tests.

You first statement here is likely a consequence of your second statement.

Only 'strong dependencies' (in R's language, i.e. from Depends and Imports
and LinkingTo in the DESCRIPTION file of the R source package) must be
installed.  As suggested packages are optional, I have argued for years that
'strong dependencies' is all we should install for (bulk) tests.

I have gotten nowhere, but as a maintainer of maybe around 100 r-cran-*
packages now have dozens removed from testings for choices I did not make.

That is, to put it mildly, frustrating.

Dirk

